# CODEOWNERS file for Tikka
# This file defines who should be automatically requested for review
# based on the files changed in a pull request.
#
# Format: <file-pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Owners can be GitHub usernames (@username) or teams (@org/team-name)
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# NOTE: This file previously used the `@maintainers` team, which is not a valid
# owner (the org has no team by that name), so ownership was never assigned.
# To add more maintainers, append their GitHub usernames to each pattern
# (or create a real `maintainers` team in the org and use `@maintainers` again).

# NOTE: Previously used @maintainers (invalid reference). Replaced with top contributor.
# Maintainers: adjust owner list to match your team/org structure.

